  "name": "lockstitch",
  "description": "Lockstitch is an incremental, stateful cryptographic construction designed for efficient symmetric-key operations including authenticated encryption, hashing, and pseudo-random function derivation. It leverages high-performance primitives like AES-128 and SHA-256 to provide a flexible protocol transcript framework similar to Merlin or Cyclist. The library focuses on performance and security on modern hardware with dedicated instructions while maintaining a minimal, misuse-resistant API.",
